{"ok":true,"codes":[],"cheat_engine":[],"mods":[{"nom":"Bypass REDlauncher or GOG Galaxy","description":"The game is DRM-free when bypassing the launcher/client. Breaks the \"Rewards\" DLC and cross-progression cloud sync. -skipStartScreen skips the \"Breaching...\" start screen. -modded is required for mods dependent on REDmod to load when skipping the launcher.}}|fix=","liens":[],"references":["https://www.gog.com/forum/cyberpunk_2077/psa_cyberpunk_2077_is_not_100_drmfree_so_far_the_rewards_dlc_is_drmed/page1"],"source":"pcgamingwiki","page":"https://www.pcgamingwiki.com/wiki/Cyberpunk_2077","consignes_url":"https://www.pcgamingwiki.com/wiki/Cyberpunk_2077#Bypass_REDlauncher_or_GOG_Galaxy","url":"https://www.pcgamingwiki.com/wiki/Cyberpunk_2077","fichiers":[],"refus":null,"refus_detail":null},{"nom":"Skip intro videos","description":"On September 2022, CD Projekt released REDmod, a free DLC that allows for easier modding. Outside of REDmod, which is designed to be used in conjunction with WolvenKit, Cyber Engine Tweaks adds basic Lua scripting support, allowing the game to be modded, it also includes a console, allowing the use of further commands. The game allows .archive and .reds (RedScript) files to be loaded. (requires RedScript and redext mods) Alongside CET, RedScript and red4ext, some mods will also make use of Input Loader and cybercmd.","liens":["https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/533","https://www.cyberpunk.net/en/modding-support","https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/2201","https://github.com/yamashi/CyberEngineTweaks","https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/1511","https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/2380","https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4575","https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/5176"],"references":[],"source":"pcgamingwiki","page":"https://www.pcgamingwiki.com/wiki/Cyberpunk_2077","consignes_url":"https://www.pcgamingwiki.com/wiki/Cyberpunk_2077#Skip_intro_videos","url":"https://www.nexusmods.co